From 5eaba685b0636b6a5ac23fe9acc0d118158ee37c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:28:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/18] feat(core): the model of a pinch and a pan: where the
 view is, and where it lands

Pure values in ArborCore, used by nothing yet (F16).

ZoomGesture is the virtual camera: a rectangle on the plane as it looks when
the fingers come down. Pinching in leads straight to what is under the pointer,
pinching out straight to everything; past either end it gives a little, against
growing resistance; a pan slides it as far as the edge of everything. `landing`
names the space the view settles on when the fingers lift.

FollowScene is what a stage shows meanwhile: one stand-in per window, and the
layout's own rule for when a window is too small to show as itself.

PanSteps turns a pan into steps to the neighbours, for where nothing can follow.

Two settings, hidden like `continuousZoom`: `panSensitivity` (1.8) and
`desktopPinchSteps` (false).
