From fbe790a3ee69c4ae666dd173787e5bd6a5c988fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:29:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/18] feat(stage): a stage can be held, and its stand-ins
 placed again and again

Two calls more for the presenter (F16), which nobody makes yet:

- `hold(_ scene:)` puts the display's stage up with every stand-in where its
  window is, and leaves it up. False where there is no stage to be had, as with
  macOS's Reduce Motion.
- `follow(_ frame:)` places the stand-ins of the scene that is held, at once.
  False if that stage has come down since: a click, a key, sleep.

In `Stage`: strips around the display's visible frame hide what rides the plane
behind the menu bar and around the Dock; the surface behind docked windows sits
in a layer of its own that rides the plane too, and is at rest unless fingers
moved it; a stand-in that is frozen goes by what was set last unless an
animation runs; a key press ends a motion as a click does.

The stand-ins for tests record scenes and frames. The fake Mac writes the
stage's lines into the log, up, held, retargeted and down, on its own clock, so
that a script can tell there as it can on a Mac.
