From aa580b7a8970fa2a66f8a546906b1900791825f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:29:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/18] test(chaos): two fingers in the chaos lab, and five
 rules for a view that follows them

`fingers <phase> <magnification> <dx> <dy>` is one update of a gesture, so that
anything can happen with the fingers down; `pinch <phase> <magnification>` still
reads, as fingers that do not slide. `reduce-motion on|off` is the Mac's setting
and outlives Arbor. Half of the walks switch `continuousZoom` on, since it ships
off and little would be seen of it.

The rules (ChaosFollow.swift): a stage that is held belongs to a gesture that is
followed; a gesture is followed on a display that is there, with a stage, and
with a timer that would end it; the stand-ins are sent somewhere finite; under
the fingers no window moves and the arrangement does not change.
