From 3e8ad1852c36a60f0c966cfa47be661f9f0403c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:41:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/18] fix(gesture): under the fingers a floating window keeps
 its own size and rides with its space

A floating window is no part of the arrangement: its frame is its person's
(QUESTIONS Q20). Its stand-in was stretched with the plane all the same. Played
in arbor-sim: a pinch in on the Desktop blew a window of 320 points up to 1017,
and the landing shrank it again, to the very frame it had never left.

Now its stand-in keeps the window's size and rides with the middle of the space
it lives on, the Desktop, or for a guest the space it opened over. The
controller asks the layout's own plan where the window would be in the two views
a gesture can bring that space back in, everything and the space on its own.
Where that is one frame the stand-in stays put while the Desktop grows around
it; where it is two, it goes straight from one to the other, never back on its
road. A slide brings it in at its own size. Where it really is counts for more
than what was foretold, so that nobody sees the stage go up.

Three tests at the controller failed first on the model as it was.
