From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:43:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/18] feat(stage): a stage that is held comes into sight with
 the first movement, and fades in

The look that ships is each app's colour and icon (QUESTIONS Q15). In that look
a stage that goes up at a touch turns the whole display into coloured cards in
one frame, and back in one frame if the fingers only rested: a flash.

So `hold` gets everything ready and shows nothing. The first `follow` that moves
anything puts the panel on screen and fades it in evenly over 160 ms. Only a stage that
is held can afford that: the real windows under it stand still for as long as it
is held, so what shows through meanwhile is what the stand-ins start from. An
ordinary motion goes up at once as before, since its windows jump underneath.

macOS-only code: it type-checks against the stand-ins, and the films of
`film-F16.sh` are what judges it. The fake Mac writes the same line into the
log, "stage in sight", for the script's check that resting fingers show nothing.
