Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:48:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/18] test(mac-shell): fingers for scripts: whole gestures
 posted on a Mac, and rehearsed on the fake one
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`witness fingers x y <move>…` plays one gesture from a list of moves: pinch,
slide, rest, and `cancel` for macOS calling it off. With a pinch among them the
slides happen during it. It reads all of its moves before it posts the first
event, since half a gesture leaves fingers down that nobody lifts, and prints
when each event was posted with the sums so far, so that a film can be held
against what the fingers had said at that moment.

The fake Mac takes the same gestures in parts, through the real GestureRouter,
and its scroll tap is there for `scrollZoom` as it is in the app. In a rehearsal
a move is made at once and then takes its time by the real clock, so that a
script that started the gesture in the background can look with the fingers down.
