+where the window would be in the view of everything and with that space on its own. Where that is one frame the stand-in stays put while the Desktop grows around it; where it is two it goes straight from one to the other. Out of view it waits beside the view, at its own size. Windows Arbor leaves alone and windows that stay in view (pinned, F49; summoned, F53) keep their place on the display (`fixed`). A summoned window that was sent away has no stand-in: no view brings it back.
