Subject: [PATCH 09/18] fix(core): a floating window out of view never starts
 in sight; the rule for tiles is the layout's to the letter

From a review of the series, each with a test that failed first.

A floating window may lie anywhere, over docked windows too. Seen from a space
that is most of everything, the Desktop is close by, and riding with its middle
the stand-in lay in the view, where the real window is not: it came into sight
with the stage. Now it waits beyond the display on the side its space is on, and
goes straight from there to where it will be. One whose space is in view while
it is not has no stand-in: nothing says which way it would come from.

`covers(under:)` called itself the layout's own rule and was not: what an app
has refused counts from more than a point under it, not half a point, and what
fills the view is what the view is on, which is never a tile.

Stand-ins are stacked by `Transition.stack`, not by a copy of it.
