From 821fddee0c66580ebbd74eea43a15bef8e26a64b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:20:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] fix(gesture): the way back leads to where a window is
 by then; the rule is about what a person asks for

A hunt of 1,500 seeds broke the rule that nothing a held stage shows is moved
behind it nine times, all of one kind: Arbor's own timers move windows too, with
nobody asking. One that strayed is put back; one whose app hung gets its place
when the app wakes. Behind the stage that harms nobody, but for one thing: the
way back led to where the window had been when the fingers came down, and the
window hopped when the stage lifted. It leads to where the window is by then. A
test failed first.

The rule now speaks of what a person asks for (a command, a key, a link, a click
on a tile), which they want to see. The same 1,500 seeds break none of the six
rules any more.
